-- title:
--   Evaluated Slice Commutation Avg Swap Terms
-- statement:
--   **Swap symmetry for averaged evaluated-slice projector terms.** Let $S$ be a symmetric projective strategy for $(m+1,q,d)$ and let $G^x$ be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family for $(m,q,d)$. Let $\mathcal D$ be the uniform distribution on evaluated-slice questions. For each question $q$, let $s_1(q),s_2(q),s_3(q),s_4(q)$ denote the outcome sums of the `BAB`, `ABA`, `BABA`, and `ABAB` scalar terms, respectively.
--
--   Swapping the two sampled question coordinates and the two field outcomes preserves the uniform law and gives
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   \mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}s_1(q)&=\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}s_2(q),\\
--   \mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}s_3(q)&=\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}s_4(q).
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   The identity is the reindexing step used in the averaged evaluated-slice commutator expansion.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.evaluatedSliceCommutation_avg_swap_terms`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/EvaluatedSliceCommutation/Averages.lean#L120-L204

